tags: ergo-p2p

A layer: the peer-to-peer protocol of the main network of Ergo, on TCP. A member of a
proof-of-work network of Ergo gives it on one address. Each message starts with the 4
magic bytes of the network, a code and a length; a message with data also has a
checksum of the data. The formal gives this frame. A node does not read the codes or
the data: it only lets an instance connect to the address. Another network of Ergo (for
example its test network) has other magic bytes, so it is another layer.

The port of the address selects the layer: nothing in TCP selects it. A layer has no
value.
=== formal
checksum=the first 4 bytes of the hash of the data
class=layer
hash.type=0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8
magic=the 4 bytes 1, 0, 2, 4 (the main network of Ergo)
message=the 4 bytes of magic, then 1 byte of code, then the length of the data as a 4-byte signed integer, big-endian, 0 or more; if the length is more than 0: 4 bytes of checksum, then the data
name=ergo-p2p
selected_by=the port of the address
transport=0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:db518cc9d8ba091449934c4a67fa56ae72c2823720e25355c092e25b823694ce
use=a node does not read the codes or the data: it only lets an instance connect to the address
